From: mscharged-port
Subject: Recharged's tournaments: the game that wins one ends with the trophy's ceremony
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

The cut online tournament ended its last game with the tournament trophy's
ceremony: the presentation script asks PRESENTATION_IS_CUP_PERSONA_WINNER
(IsCupPersonaWinner: online, GM_ONLINE_TOURNAMENT and the last playoff
round), then Presentation::LoadNis loads <trophy>_<name> (the disc has all
ten, mushroomcup_win_home_2.nis to nintendocup_win_home_2.nis, beside the
Strikers Cup's), with the trophy's model from
AsyncLoadingManager::LoadTrophyTemplates.

Recharged's tournaments play their sets as RANKED matches. Two hooks let
them have the same ending without the game's tournament mode:
mscharged_tweak_tournament_trophy gives the trophy for a game won by a
side (the presentation then takes the persona's ceremony), and
mscharged_tweak_tournament_trophy_template the trophy whose model the
match loads. That model goes by the disc's names: the cut branch asks for
Trophy<persona>Cup, which only the Next Level trophy is called.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
--- a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
@@ -280,6 +280,13 @@ bool mscharged_tweak_training_item_giant(void);
 // once, the message of the popup that says so.
 bool mscharged_tweak_online_locked(void);
 const unsigned short* mscharged_tweak_take_online_lock_message(void);
+// Recharged's tournaments (tweak patch 0076): the game that wins one ends
+// with the tournament trophy's ceremony, as the cut online tournament's
+// would have. The trophy (a cup persona, 0 to 9) for a game won by
+// `winner_side` (0 home, 1 away), or -1 for the usual end; and the trophy
+// whose model the matches of a set that may end the tournament load, or -1.
+int mscharged_tweak_tournament_trophy(int winner_side);
+int mscharged_tweak_tournament_trophy_template(void);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
